<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 6 July, from 1189 to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1189">1189 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">837 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard the Lionheart becomes King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry II died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinon">Chinon</a>, and his son Richard succeeded him. Famed as a crusader against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, Richard spent barely six months of his ten-year reign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1415">1415 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">611 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jan Hus is burned at the stake in Constance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Czech reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a>, condemned as a heretic by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a> despite a promise of safe conduct, was burned. His death provoked the Hussite revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> a century before Luther.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1483">1483 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">543 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard III is crowned at Westminster Abbey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucester">Gloucester</a>, was crowned after his nephew Edward V was declared illegitimate. Two years later his death at Bosworth ended Plantagenet rule and brought the Tudors to the throne.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1685">1685 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">341 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Monmouth's rebellion is crushed at Sedgemoor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Royal troops routed the Duke of Monmouth's rebel army at Sedgemoor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a>, often called the last pitched battle on English soil. Judge Jeffreys's 'Bloody Assizes' followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German ambassador Mirbach is assassinated in Moscow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-revolutionary-party">Socialist Revolutionaries</a> shot Count Wilhelm von Mirbach in the German embassy, hoping to wreck the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brest-belarus">Brest-Litovsk</a> peace. Their uprising was crushed and the Bolsheviks became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s sole ruling party.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire sweeps a circus big top in Hartford, killing 167</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ringling Bros. tent, waterproofed with paraffin and petrol, caught fire during a matinee in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hartford-connecticut">Hartford, Connecticut</a>. At least 167 people died, many of them children, prompting tighter fire-safety rules.</p></div></li></ol>
